      "message": "Yeah, you are right. There is no need to clear `fpscr` variable, because it\u0027s checked after FPU interrupt was triggered (`fpu_irq_handled` is true).\n\nPlease note that `fpu_irq()` handler clears FPSCR (it\u0027s cleared on stack in line 35, when we return from exception, we copy FPSCR from stack to the register), so `clear_fpscr()` was not necessary, but since you want to run this tests on chips that don\u0027t have FPU interrupt, this function becomes essential.\n\nNIT: If you find this useful, you can add some comments in code.",
